{"title":"2025 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be complex numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d938fc4d264b78693b353d9e47e2596bfdb5f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a|=|b|=|c|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />. Suppose that the three summations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f04ab0e294ce7f0658ea7fbf97ea5223f44ddec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=0}^5 a^ib^{5-i}, \\ \\sum_{i=0}^7 b^ic^{7-i}, \\ \\text{and} \\  \\sum_{i=0}^{11} c^ia^{11-i}\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"50\" /> are all nonzero real numbers. Find the number of possible ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4b6ed83eac27565bd18980bb9bce600be67b21e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ab)^{5/2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"23\" /> divides the first sum, which you can see by pairing off <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/5407a8700cb4be78884222dfc8143be4fe3da09b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^5 + b^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a597c3abbfeb323eaca67219ab709163a36d74f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab^4 + a^4b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />, etc and visualizing each of their sum in the complex plane. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43d32c5d8732422c645e96eb6cbb054ecbe7c21e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a| = |b| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" /> and this sum is real, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/1087bef0266c7c49ef12d0a748fa466d789e3890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ab)^5 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"21\" />. Similarly, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d639805ff65b68e062584495c5afe9750829f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(bc)^7 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f3a85a5cd0f61be69142d858dd2d72c6a69d111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ac)^{11} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"21\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4dd4a3ee033662cdd95de1f1ce6349c8029284bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> ways to choose values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f50cdf5332ac9bcea5dc482359acc42f37fe064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab, bc, ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> and each system will have two solutions, so there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c06915b34e84219b888157579a31acf097ff50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 11 = \\boxed{770}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"149\" height=\"25\" /> solutions. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~ostriches88 &amp; Sedro\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018033730\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 68/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3146/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35309:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018033730 and revision id 273940. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}